# Scheduled tasks of the image, run by `apercura scheduler` (supercronic). Times are UTC.
#
# Expirations, reminders, the email outbox, next free slots and purges. Every sub-job holds a
# Postgres advisory lock, so a run that lasts longer than five minutes is harmless.
*/5 * * * * apercura jobs:tick

# Cache warm-up: the next slice of the walk of the sitemap URLs against the app
# (INTERNAL_APP_URL), highest-value pages first, at most WARM_CACHE_MAX_SECONDS (240) per run,
# two minutes after jobs:tick. A walk stops at its budget (what half of the page cache holds,
# WARM_CACHE_BUDGET_URLS). Starts over after a deploy (new build) or an import; idle once the
# walk is over. Off with WARM_CACHE=false. Its advisory lock keeps one run at a time.
2-59/5 * * * * apercura jobs:tick warm

# Open data import, every Monday at 03:00 UTC. ETL_SCHEDULE_ARGS narrows it, e.g.
# `--department 75`; empty imports all of France. Exit codes: 1 failed, 2 blocked (see
# docs/data-import.md).
0 3 * * 1 apercura etl:fr $ETL_SCHEDULE_ARGS

# Austria's open data (Vienna, Styria, Salzburg), every Monday at 05:30 UTC, after France's
# import (both take the same advisory lock: one import at a time). ETL_AT_SCHEDULE_ARGS
# narrows it, e.g. `--sources wien`. Exit codes: 1 failed, 2 blocked, 3 imported without a
# list that could not be fetched or read (see docs/data-import.md, "Austria").
30 5 * * 1 apercura etl:at $ETL_AT_SCHEDULE_ARGS

# The United Kingdom's NHS open data (ODS for England and Wales, Public Health Scotland, the
# Business Services Organisation), every Monday at 06:30 UTC, after Austria's import (the same
# advisory lock: one import at a time). ETL_GB_SCHEDULE_ARGS narrows it, e.g.
# `--sources ods-gp,ods-branches`. Exit codes: 1 failed, 2 blocked, 3 imported without a list
# that could not be fetched or read (see docs/data-import.md, "United Kingdom").
30 6 * * 1 apercura etl:gb $ETL_GB_SCHEDULE_ARGS

# Czechia's register of healthcare providers (NRPZS, ÚZIS, published monthly), every Monday at
# 07:30 UTC, after the UK's import (the same advisory lock: one import at a time); an unchanged
# export is skipped. ETL_CZ_SCHEDULE_ARGS adds flags. Exit codes: 1 failed (the export could not
# be fetched or read), 2 blocked (see docs/data-import.md, "Czechia").
30 7 * * 1 apercura etl:cz $ETL_CZ_SCHEDULE_ARGS

# Spain's register of health centres (REGCESS, Ministerio de Sanidad, extracts published
# monthly), every Monday at 08:30 UTC, after Czechia's import (the same advisory lock: one import
# at a time); unchanged extracts are skipped. ETL_ES_SCHEDULE_ARGS narrows it, e.g.
# `--sources regcess-e`. Exit codes: 1 failed, 2 blocked, 3 imported without an extract that
# could not be fetched or read (see docs/data-import.md, "Spain").
30 8 * * 1 apercura etl:es $ETL_ES_SCHEDULE_ARGS

# Italy's Ministry of Health open data (pharmacies and parapharmacies, published daily; the
# yearly hospital bed counts), every Monday at 09:30 UTC, after the other imports (the same
# advisory lock: one import at a time); unchanged lists are skipped. ETL_IT_SCHEDULE_ARGS narrows
# it, e.g. `--sources farmacie`. Exit codes: 1 failed, 2 blocked, 3 imported without a list that
# could not be fetched or read (see docs/data-import.md, "Italy").
30 9 * * 1 apercura etl:it $ETL_IT_SCHEDULE_ARGS
# Germany's open data (the statistical offices' yearly directory of hospitals and of prevention
# and rehabilitation clinics, Thuringia's and Brandenburg's pharmacy lists), on the 2nd of every
# month at 22:30 UTC, when no other import runs (the same advisory lock: one import at a time).
# Unchanged files end the run after their download (a few MB). ETL_DE_SCHEDULE_ARGS narrows it,
# e.g. `--sources khv,rhv`. Exit codes: 1 failed, 2 blocked, 3 imported without a source that
# could not be fetched or read (see docs/data-import.md, "Germany").
30 22 2 * * apercura etl:de $ETL_DE_SCHEDULE_ARGS
